<example>
<input>
project_type: mobile_app
detail_level: detailed
output_format: phases_table

A fitness tracking mobile app for iOS and Android. Users sign up with
email or Apple/Google SSO, log workouts manually or via Apple Health /
Google Fit, see weekly progress charts, and receive daily reminders.
The app integrates with Stripe for a premium tier (advanced analytics,
custom training plans). Target launch: 4 months.
</input>
<output>
| phase                         | duration_weeks | cost_eur | confidence_pct |
|-------------------------------|----------------|----------|----------------|
| Discovery & UX design         | 3              | 12000    | 80             |
| Auth (email + SSO)            | 2              | 8000     | 85             |
| Workout logging core          | 4              | 18000    | 70             |
| HealthKit / Google Fit sync   | 3              | 14000    | 60             |
| Charts & dashboards           | 2              | 9000     | 75             |
| Stripe + premium gating       | 2              | 9000     | 80             |
| Push notifications & QA       | 2              | 7000     | 75             |
| **Totals**                    | **18**         | **77000**| —              |

Assumptions:
- Single product team of 1 PM, 2 mobile devs, 1 backend dev, 1 designer.
- React Native or Flutter; cross-platform from a single codebase.
- Stripe Checkout (hosted), no custom in-app purchase yet.

Risks:
- HealthKit / Google Fit edge cases on older OS versions could add 1–2 weeks.
- App Store / Play Store review cycles not modelled in the totals.
</output>
</example>

<example>
<input>
project_type: web_saas
detail_level: medium
output_format: line_items
</input>
<output>
- **Auth + multi-tenant org model** — 3 weeks, 13000 EUR, 75% confidence.
  Driver: SSO with SAML for enterprise prospects requires extra setup.
- **Inventory CRUD + bulk import** — 4 weeks, 16000 EUR, 80% confidence.
  Driver: CSV import with validation is the bulk of effort, not the CRUD.
- **Reporting dashboards (3 boards)** — 3 weeks, 12000 EUR, 70% confidence.
  Driver: charting library integration and aggregation queries.
- **Stripe billing + plan tiers** — 2 weeks, 9000 EUR, 85% confidence.
  Driver: well-trodden path with Stripe Checkout.
- **Admin tools and audit log** — 2 weeks, 8000 EUR, 75% confidence.
  Driver: required for enterprise sales, often underestimated.
- **QA + onboarding hardening** — 2 weeks, 6000 EUR, 80% confidence.
  Driver: production polish before the first paying customer.
- **Totals** — 16 weeks, 64000 EUR.
</output>
</example>

<example>
<input>
project_type: internal_tool
detail_level: summary
output_format: narrative
</input>
<output>
A CRM-style internal tool for the sales team should be deliverable in
roughly 6 to 8 weeks at a cost between 22000 and 30000 EUR, assuming a
small team of one full-stack developer and a part-time designer.

The bulk of the effort lies in modelling the contact and pipeline
entities, integrating with the existing email provider, and giving the
sales reps a fast list view with inline editing. Reporting can stay
minimal in the first release — pivot tables in the existing BI tool
will cover most needs while the internal product matures.

The main risks are integration scope creep (every sales rep will ask
for "just one more" integration) and the temptation to add custom
permissions per user role. Both can be deferred to a second release.
</output>
</example>

